28	COMP-1768302393192-0a5k2ivbh	653.003.04	743ef9d1-841a-11ed-aa7c-7003bca91a86	\N	\N	WO-1768302478843-emi3og2kh	MKR-IN-00085-653.003.04-2026-001	AE Cylinder Liner Inspection - 1M	Inspection	2026-01-13	\N	3rd Engineer	Chief Engineer	2026-01-13	Approved	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Liner Condition (Visual / Indirect)\r\n\r\nCheck for abnormal scavenge space condition (if accessible).\r\n\r\nLook for signs of scuffing, scoring, or polishing (based on inspection ports or trend data).\r\n\r\nMonitor liner condition through performance parameters if direct access is not possible.\r\n\r\n2. Lubrication\r\n\r\nVerify cylinder lubrication rate (if applicable) is as per maker’s recommendation.\r\n\r\nCheck lube oil distribution and absence of oil starvation signs.\r\n\r\nReview lube oil consumption trends.\r\n\r\n3. Cooling & Sealing\r\n\r\nMonitor jacket water temperature and pressure related to cylinder No.01.\r\n\r\nCheck for cooling water leakage into cylinder or crankcase.\r\n\r\nVerify condition of liner sealing arrangements (indirect observation).	"[]"	\N	f	2026-01-14 06:33:55.045311
