\n\r\n3. Valves (Inlet / Exhaust / Indicator / Starting if fitted)\r\n\r\nInspect exhaust valve area for gas leakage or overheating.\r\n\r\nCheck inlet valve area for abnormal noise or leakage.\r\n\r\nInspect indicator and starting valves for tightness and free operation.\r\n\r\nEnsure valve caps and safety devices are properly fitted.	Chief Engineer	Engine	[]	[]	{"ppeRequirements":[],"permitRequirements":[],"otherRequirements":[]}	vessel	651.002.AA	\N	\N	No	t	\N	\N	2026-01-13 11:06:58.369504	\N	2026-01-13 11:06:59.134
JOB-1768302820637-qr1n8r9a4	743feb08-841a-11ed-aa7c-7003bca91a86	COMP-1768302796271-7kv8askj7	554.005.01	Condensers No.01	MKR-IN-00052	Provision Ref. Condensers Pressure Switch, Visual Check - 1Y	2nd Engineer	Inspection	Calendar	\N	1	Years	\N	\N	\N	\N	20-Jan-2025	20-Jan-2026	\N	\N	Medium	Yes	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nJOB REFERENCE DETAILS\r\n===================\r\nManual Name: 2F-16 UNIT TYPE PROV. REF. CHAMBER;5303.pdf\r\nPdf Page No: 92\r\nChapter: 3.inspection\r\n\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Check the pressure switch by stopping the condenser water.( High Side)\r\n3. Check the pressure switch by closing the condenser water outlet valve.( Low Side)	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nJOB REFERENCE DETAILS\r\n===================\r\nManual Name: 2F-16 UNIT TYPE PROV. REF. CHAMBER;5303.pdf\r\nPdf Page No: 92\r\nChapter: 3.inspection\r\n\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Check the pressure switch by stopping the condenser water.( High Side)\r\n3. Check the pressure switch by closing the condenser water outlet valve.( Low Side)	Chief Engineer	Engine	[]	[]	{"ppeRequirements":[],"permitRequirements":[],"otherRequirements":[]}	vessel	554.005.AA	\N	\N	Yes	t	\N	\N	2026-01-13 11:13:40.637789	\N	2026-01-13 11:13:40.646
JOB-1768302820651-lqd4vi7ed	743feb08-841a-11ed-aa7c-7003bca91a86	COMP-1768302796119-c9p1lpswb	601.001	Main diesel engine, compl.	MKR-IN-00074	Main Engine General Inspection - 1M	2nd Engineer	Inspection	Calendar	\N	1	Months	\N	\N	\N	\N	02-Dec-2025	02-Jan-2026	\N	\N	Low	No	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\nCarry out a complete monthly inspection of the main diesel engine to ensure safe, reliable, and efficient operation. The inspection includes mechanical, lubrication, cooling, fuel, air, exhaust, control, and safety systems, with emphasis on early detection of wear, leakage, abnormal vibration, or deviation from normal operating parameters.\r\n\r\n1. General Condition\r\n\r\nInspect engine exterior for oil, fuel, water, or exhaust gas leakage.\r\n\r\nCheck for abnormal vibration, noise, or overheating.\r\n\r\nEnsure foundation bolts, holding-down bolts, and chocks show no abnormal condition.\r\n\r\n2. Lubrication System\r\n\r\nCheck sump oil level and condition.\r\n\r\nReview lube oil pressure, temperature, and differential pressure across filters.\r\n\r\nInspect lube oil filters and coolers for leakage.\r\n\r\nVerify oil mist detector operation and alarm status.\r\n\r\n3. Fuel System\r\n\r\nInspect fuel pumps, injectors, and fuel lines for leakage.\r\n\r\nCheck fuel oil pressure, temperature, and viscosity (as applicable).\r\n\r\nDrain and check fuel filters and settling system as required.\r\n\r\n4. Cooling Water System\r\n\r\nCheck jacket water pressure, temperature, and expansion tank level.\r\n\r\nInspect freshwater and seawater pumps for leakage.\r\n\r\nVerify cooler condition and seawater inlet/outlet temperatures.\r\n\r\n5. Air & Exhaust System\r\n\r\nInspect turbocharger casing, air inlet filters, and ducting.\r\n\r\nCheck exhaust manifold for leakage, cracks, or insulation damage.\r\n\r\nMonitor exhaust gas temperatures for cylinder deviation.\r\n\r\n6. Starting & Control System\r\n\r\nCheck starting air pressure and drain receivers.\r\n\r\nInspect starting valves and control air system.\r\n\r\nVerify correct operation of engine control system, telegraph, and safety interlocks.\r\n\r\n7. Safety & Protection Devices\r\n\r\nTest safety devices as per PMS schedule:\r\n\r\nOverspeed trip\r\n\r\nLow lube oil pressure alarm\r\n\r\nHigh jacket water temperature alarm\r\n\r\nVerify crankcase relief valves condition.\r\n\r\n8. Performance Monitoring\r\n\r\nRecord engine RPM, load, and fuel consumption.\r\n\r\nReview trends for lube oil consumption and exhaust temperatures.\r\n\r\nCompare readings with previous records.	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\nCarry out a complete monthly inspection of the main diesel engine to ensure safe, reliable, and efficient operation. The inspection includes mechanical, lubrication, cooling, fuel, air, exhaust, control, and safety systems, with emphasis on early detection of wear, leakage, abnormal vibration, or deviation from normal operating parameters.\r\n\r\n1. General Condition\r\n\r\nInspect engine exterior for oil, fuel, water, or exhaust gas leakage.\r\n\r\nCheck for abnormal vibration, noise, or overheating.\r\n\r\nEnsure foundation bolts, holding-down bolts, and chocks show no abnormal condition.\r\n\r\n2. Lubrication System\r\n\r\nCheck sump oil level and condition.\r\n\r\nReview lube oil pressure, temperature, and differential pressure across filters.\r\n\r\nInspect lube oil filters and coolers for leakage.\r\n\r\nVerify oil mist detector operation and alarm status.\r\n\r\n3. Fuel System\r\n\r\nInspect fuel pumps, injectors, and fuel lines for leakage.\r\n\r\nCheck fuel oil pressure, temperature, and viscosity (as applicable).\r\n\r\nDrain and check fuel filters and settling system as required.\r\n\r\n4. Cooling Water System\r\n\r\nCheck jacket water pressure, temperature, and expansion tank level.\r\n\r\nInspect freshwater and seawater pumps for leakage.\r\n\r\nVerify cooler condition and seawater inlet/outlet temperatures.\r\n\r\n5. Air & Exhaust System\r\n\r\nInspect turbocharger casing, air inlet filters, and ducting.\r\n\r\nCheck exhaust manifold for leakage, cracks, or insulation damage.\r\n\r\nMonitor exhaust gas temperatures for cylinder deviation.\r\n\r\n6. Starting & Control System\r\n\r\nCheck starting air pressure and drain receivers.\r\n\r\nInspect starting valves and control air system.\r\n\r\nVerify correct operation of engine control system, telegraph, and safety interlocks.\r\n\r\n7. Safety & Protection Devices\r\n\r\nTest safety devices as per PMS schedule:\r\n\r\nOverspeed trip\r\n\r\nLow lube oil pressure alarm\r\n\r\nHigh jacket water temperature alarm\r\n\r\nVerify crankcase relief valves condition.\r\n\r\n8. Performance Monitoring\r\n\r\nRecord engine RPM, load, and fuel consumption.\r\n\r\nReview trends for lube oil consumption and exhaust temperatures.\r\n\r\nCompare readings with previous records.	Chief Engineer	Engine	[]	[]	{"ppeRequirements":[],"permitRequirements":[],"otherRequirements":[]}	vessel	601.001.AA	\N	\N	No	t	\N	\N	2026-01-13 11:13:40.652673	\N	2026-01-13 11:13:40.652673
