JOB-1768375697502-3ijpl6vm3	7440571a-841a-11ed-aa7c-7003bca91a86	COMP-1768374767830-uxleqdvg1	601.018	ME crankcases	MKR-IN-00077	Main Engine – Crankcase Inspection - 1M	2nd Engineer	Inspection	Calendar	\N	1	Months	\N	\N	\N	\N	02-Dec-2025	02-Jan-2026	\N	\N	Low	No	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Crankcase General Condition\r\n\r\nInspect crankcase internally for cleanliness, sludge accumulation, or metallic debris.\r\n\r\nCheck for oil leakage, cracks, or abnormal discoloration.\r\n\r\nEnsure crankcase doors, inspection covers, and securing bolts are in good condition.\r\n\r\n2. Bearings & Rotating Parts\r\n\r\nInspect main bearings and crankpin bearings (visual access only) for signs of overheating or wipe.\r\n\r\nCheck crankshaft webs, journals, and fillets for abnormal marks or scoring.\r\n\r\nInspect connecting rod big-end area for abnormal condition.\r\n\r\n3. Lubrication & Oil Mist\r\n\r\nVerify lube oil spray pattern and oil return passages.\r\n\r\nCheck crankcase lube oil temperature and pressure.\r\n\r\nInspect oil mist detector (OMD) sensors, piping, and alarm status.\r\n\r\n4. Crankcase Ventilation & Safety\r\n\r\nEnsure crankcase relief valves are clean, free, and properly secured.\r\n\r\nCheck flame arresters and relief valve covers for damage.\r\n\r\nVerify no obstruction in crankcase ventilation arrangements.\r\n\r\n5. Trend & Condition Monitoring\r\n\r\nReview bearing temperature trends and vibration data.\r\n\r\nCompare current observations with previous inspection records.\r\n\r\nReview lube oil analysis reports for wear metal indication.	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Crankcase General Condition\r\n\r\nInspect crankcase internally for