JOB-1768381234221-qhy0488rh	744535d0-841a-11ed-aa7c-7003bca91a86	COMP-1768381197031-giasm3ygh	652.004.01	AE 2 AE pistons And Connecting Rod No.01	MKR-OV-00025	AE Pistons and Connecting Rods Overhaul - 4000H	3rd Engineer	Overhaul	Running Hours	\N	4000	Hours	4000	\N	\N	\N	20-Dec-2015	\N	0	4000	Low	No	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Pistons\r\n\r\nRemove pistons from cylinder liners (if applicable) for detailed inspection.\r\n\r\nInspect piston crowns, skirts, and grooves for cracks, scuffing, scoring, or overheating.\r\n\r\nMeasure piston-to-liner clearance and compare with maker’s tolerances.\r\n\r\nInspect piston rings for wear, free movement, and proper seating in grooves.\r\n\r\nClean carbon deposits and inspect oil cooling passages for blockage.\r\n\r\n2. Connecting Rods\r\n\r\nRemove and inspect connecting rods for cracks, bending, or discoloration.\r\n\r\nCheck big-end bearings for wear; measure clearance and compare with manufacturer’s limits.\r\n\r\nInspect securing nuts, bolts, and locking devices; torque as per specification.\r\n\r\nExamine small-end bearings and piston pin for wear or abnormal play.\r\n\r\n3. Lubrication & Oil System\r\n\r\nInspect lubrication lines and ensure unobstructed oil flow to pistons and connecting rods.\r\n\r\nCheck oil feed pipes and connections for leaks, corrosion, or damage.\r\n\r\nVerify oil filter and purifier performance; check for metallic debris.\r\n\r\n4. Cylinder Liner Interaction\r\n\r\nCheck piston ring alignment and interaction with cylinder liner.\r\n\r\nInspect liner condition (scoring, wear, corrosion) associated with piston operation.	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Pistons\r\n\r\nRemove pistons fr