WO-1768375973120-e21p53jyh	7440571a-841a-11ed-aa7c-7003bca91a86	ME Cylinder Covers W/Valves No.06	601.002.06	JOB-1768375697108-vju6zh1n5	MKR-IN-00075-601.002.06-2026-001	Planned	MKR-IN-00075-601.002.06-2026-001	\N	Main Engine – Cylinder Covers with Valves Inspection - 4000H	2nd Engineer	\N	Overdue	\N	\N	\N	Inspection	\N	Running Hours	4000	Hours	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	4000	6000	No	Low	SAFETY PROCEDURE (COMPANY)\r\n===========================\r\nEnsure compliance with safety procedures according to the company policy and requirements.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\n===========\r\n1. Cylinder Cover Condition\r\n\r\nInspect cylinder cover externally for cracks, corrosion, or hot spots.\r\n\r\nCheck for leakage of combustion gas, cooling water, or lube oil.\r\n\r\nVerify tightening condition of cover studs and nuts (visual/record check).\r\n\r\n2. Cooling Water Passages\r\n\r\nCheck cooling water inlet and outlet connections for leakage.\r\n\r\nMonitor jacket water temperature differences across cylinders.\r\n\r\nInspect for signs of scaling or blockage (based on temperature trend).\r\n\r\n3. Valves (Exhaust / Inlet / Starting / Indicator)\r\n\r\nInspect exhaust valve housing area for gas leakage or abnormal heating.\r\n\r\nCheck operation of:\r\n\r\nExhaust valve (opening/closing behavior via parameters)\r\n\r\nStarting air valve (no leakage during normal running)\r\n\r\nIndicator valve (tightness and free operation)\r\n\r\nEnsure valve caps and securing devices are properly fitted.\r\n\r\n4. Valve Actuation System\r\n\r\nInspect hydraulic or mechanical valve actuation components.\r\n\r\nCheck for oil leakage at pipes, flanges, and fittings.\r\n\r\nMonitor hydraulic oil pressure and temperature (if applicable).\r\n\r\n1. General Condition\r\n\r\nInspect engine exterior for oil, fuel, water, or exhaust gas leakage.\r\n\r\nCheck for abnormal vibration, noise, or overheating.\r\n\r\nEnsure foundation bolts, holding-down bolts, and chocks show no abnormal condition.\r\n\r\n2. Lubrication System\r\n\r\nCheck sump oil level and condition.\r\n\r\nReview lube oil pressure, temperature, and differential pressure across filters.\r\n\r\nInspect lube oil filters and coolers for leakage.\r\n\r\nVerify oil mist detector operation and alarm status.\r\n\r\n3. Fuel System\r\n\r\nInspect fuel pumps, injectors, and fuel lines for leakage.\r\n\r\nCheck fuel oil pressure, temperature, and viscosity (as applicable).\r\n\r\nDrain and check fuel filters and settling system as required.\r\n\r\n4. Cooling Water System\r\n\r\nCheck jacket water pressure, temperature, and expansion tank level.\r\n\r\nInspect freshwater and seawater pumps for leakage.\r\n\r\nVerify cooler condition and seawater inlet/outlet temperatures.\r\n\r\n5. Air & Exhaust System\r\n\r\nInspect turbocharger casing, air inlet filters, and ducting.\r\n\r\nCheck exhaust manifold for leakage, cracks, or insulation damage.\r\n\r\nMonitor exhaust gas temperatures for cylinder deviation.\r\n\r\n6. Starting & Control System\r\n\r\nCheck starting air pressure and drain receivers.\r\n\r\nInspect starting valves and control air system.\r\n\r\nVerify correct operation of engine control system, telegraph, and safety interlocks.\r\n\r\n7. Safety & Protection Devices\r\n\r\nTest safety devices as per PMS schedule:\r\n\r\nOverspeed trip\r\n\r\nLow lube oil pressure alarm\r\n\r\nHigh jacket water temperature alarm\r\n\r\nVerify crankcase relief valves condition.\r\n\r\n8. Performance Monitoring\r\n\r\nRecord engine RPM, load, and fuel consumption.\r\n\r\nReview trends for lube oil consumption and exhaust temperatures.\r\n\r\nCompare readings with previous records.	vessel	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	4000	Engine	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	[]	[]	{"ppeRequirements":[],"permitRequirements":[],"otherRequirements":[]}	[]	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	RH	4000.00	3280.00	4000.00	6000.00	0.00	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-01-14 07:32:53.122104	2026-01-14 07:33:53.09
